.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
.\" Hand-written (the program has no clap definitions): what the engine
.\" starts it with, and what a service manager runs.
.TH VELARX-REGISTRY 1 "" "velarx" "Velarx"
.SH NAME
velarx\-registry \- the registry fetcher of velarx
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B velarx\-registry
.RB [ \-\-config
.IR FILE " | " \-\-config\-fd
.IR N ]
.RB [ \-\-listen\-fd
.IR N " | " \-\-varlink\-fd
.IR N ]
.RB [ \-\-staging\-fd
.IR N ]
.RB [ \-\-idle\-exit
.IR SECS " | " \-\-shared
.IR PATH ]
.RB [ \-\-self\-test ]
.br
.B velarx\-registry pull\-worker
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B velarx\-registry
is the process that talks to the registries for velarx.  It is installed
next to
.BR velarx (1),
and the engine finds it there (or where
.I registry_path
of
.BR velarx.conf (5)
says) and starts it under the lock of its socket (no service manager runs
it).
It serves
.B org.velarx.Fetcher
(the pull of manifests, tables of contents and files, written into the
staging directory of the store) and
.B org.velarx.Pusher
(the blobs and manifests of a push, placed at the repository of its scope) and
.B org.velarx.Registry
(login, tags and search), and holds the credentials
only of the registries it is asked about.
.PP
A connection is given its scope once, by
.B Open
(a second one is refused, so is any other call before it), and
.B Connect
and
.B Renew
act on that scope only, for both interfaces alike: the credentials of a
connection are never those of another client.
.PP
It confines itself before it serves anything (Landlock, seccomp, no
capability but the one that reads) and refuses to run on a kernel that
cannot enforce all of it.  The requests to the registries and the
decompression are made by its confined workers,
.BR "velarx\-registry pull\-worker" ,
which it starts through a spawner process forked before the confinement:
this is not a command for users.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-config " FILE"
The configuration file (default: the one of
.BR velarx.conf (5)).
.TP
.BI \-\-config\-fd " N"
The configuration as JSON in the descriptor
.IR N ,
given by the engine that started the process.
.TP
.BI \-\-listen\-fd " N"
The listening socket, bound by the starter.
.TP
.BI \-\-varlink\-fd " N"
The one connection to serve, which the engine of a command started the
process for; it leaves when that connection is closed.
.TP
.BI \-\-staging\-fd " N"
The staging directory of the store: the only place the process writes.
.TP
.BI \-\-idle\-exit " SECS"
Leave when no connection was open for this long.
.TP
.BI \-\-shared " PATH"
The socket is at
.IR PATH :
leave when the last connection is closed and take the socket away.
.TP
.B \-\-self\-test
Confine the process, try from inside what the confinement allows and
refuses and print the results as JSON; nothing is served.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version and the commit of the build.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR velarx (1),
.BR velarx\-dir (1),
.BR velarx.conf (5)
